      "side": 1,
      "message": "Could the message say what fails without this patch? As far as I can see, it only affects a handler in another process with a larger address space: a native handler serving a 4KB process gets `-EINVAL` for any source above `TASK_SIZE_4KB` (1 \u003c\u003c 39), which is where native mmap() usually places its buffers. It would also help to say that the length check doesn\u0027t change.",
