      "side": 1,
      "message": "Agreed that the source should be checked against the caller: `mfill_atomic_copy()` reads it with `copy_from_user()` from `current-\u003emm`, not from `ctx-\u003emm`.\n\nIt looks like `validate_unaligned_range()` already does the rest. Its `len \u0026 ~PAGE_MASK` check uses the destination page size, because `userfaultfd_ioctl()` runs under `P3S_CONTEXT_REMOTE_MM(ctx-\u003emm)` since aosp/4312528, so `mm_pte_size(dst_mm)` gives the same result. Would passing `current-\u003emm` to the existing call work for you?\n\n```\n\tret \u003d validate_unaligned_range(current-\u003emm, uffdio_copy.src,\n\t\t\t\t       uffdio_copy.len);\n```\n\nThat would keep the change to one line, plus a comment on why the caller\u0027s mm is used.",
      "isAi": true,
      "revId": "4e1a562b2b2d5d8af8efffde39cb18443cbc32c4",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
