      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think the untagging changes native processes too. Since `2ef5d7245d9c` (`\"mm: userfaultfd: check for start + len overflow in validate_range\"`), a tagged `src` fails with `-EINVAL` for every caller, because `validate_unaligned_range()` compares it with `task_size`.\n\nAccepting it may well match `Documentation/arch/arm64/tagged-address-abi.rst`, which only excludes `range.start`, `start` and `dst`, but it isn\u0027t specific to P3S. Would it be OK to drop it here, together with the tagged source in `userfaultfd_remote_ppps.c` (aosp/4367986), and send it upstream separately if it\u0027s needed?",
